|term[resolution-engine]
  :status settled
  :subject-field addressing
  :layer framing-vocabulary
  :gloss What performs resolution, relative to a perspective; owes the actor six obligations.
  :see-also [@perspective @progressive-routing]
  |designation resolution-engine
    :status preferred
    :channel prose
  |designation engine
    :status admitted
    :channel prose
  |definition
    :defined-by @def-cardinality-and-resolution
    :anchor engine-and-perspective
    :projection paraphrase
    Resolution is not a property of the reference act — it is performed by a resolution engine relative to a perspective. The same act may legitimately resolve differently under different engines; someone must own each hop, and the engine is the composite owner.
  |rel :kind resolves :to @reference-act :card *
  |rel :kind relative-to :to @perspective :card 1
  |invariant
    Owes the six obligations: typed outcomes; descriptors preserved; never a silent best-guess; fetch-verification when carried; weak resolution disclosed ([[DECISIONS#d6-found-but-weakly|D6 found-but-weakly]]); zero only from a completed perspective ([[DECISIONS#d7-completed-perspective|D7 completed-perspective]]).
  |note :audience maintainer
    Store-model candidate identity (disc-store-composition-model): a bound store composition IS an engine — composing the perspective produces the executing thing.
